                <pb facs="0822" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg734"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Eddy.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee instructs Mr. Eddy to ascertain whether the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Arabia</hi> has been taken to Vladivostok, whether a prize court has ben
                    established there, and whether that vessel is charged with carrying contraband
                    of war, and if this be the case, to report particulars.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
